\0
Several years after the Freedom Guard destroyed the Dessicator weapon on Corlbad, Imperium scientists were able to duplicate the weapon. In order to avoid losing the weapon again, the Dessicator was developed as a series of components on a number of worlds. All aspects of the research were duplicated, and only General Trilkin was aware of the sites of all phases of development.  When all was ready, Imperium fleets brought the separate components to Monat for final implementation. 
\1
The Dessicator has been assembled and is ready to be deployed. The Freedom Guard has launched a massive attack on Monat in an attempt to destroy the weapon. Repel the Freedom Guard from the planet. Execute their forces to a man. Destroy every vehicle. Level every structure. Their ruin is at hand. 
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
-->  Eliminate all Freedom Guard units and\n
\s\s\s\s buildings
\2
The summit is within your reach. Prepare yourself, for the real battle is at hand.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
Entrenched Imperium forces successfully defended the Dessicator against seemingly inexhaustible tides of Freedom Guard troops. Severe casualties were suffered both sides, but the Imperium ultimately decimated the Freedom Guard invaders. The completed Dessicator was taken by General Trilkin, and his command fleet headed for Strata, one of the Freedom Guard's few remaining strongholds, where they intended to implement the Dessicator and deal a death blow to the insurgent cause.
\3
Your determination is lacking. Steel yourself and try again.


